<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450395" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 3 — Image Size is Larger than 100 Pixels</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a paragraph that introduces a large architecture diagram whose width and height attributes are</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>architecture</keyword>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>width</keyword>
        <keyword>height</keyword>
        <keyword>system</keyword>
        <keyword>overview</keyword>
        <indexterm>architecture</indexterm>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
        <indexterm>width</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider a paragraph that introduces a large architecture diagram whose width and height attributes are both larger than 100 pixels.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Image larger than 100 pixels</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_oxx_mj4_lkc">
&lt;p>The following diagram illustrates the overall system architecture.&lt;/p>
&lt;img src="media/system_architecture_overview.png" alt="System architecture overview" width="1024" height="768"/></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_cgl_4j4_lkc">
&lt;p>The following diagram illustrates the overall system architecture.&lt;/p>
&lt;fig>
  &lt;title>System Architecture Overview&lt;/title>
  &lt;image href="media/system_architecture_overview.png" placement="break" width="13" height="10">
    &lt;alt>System architecture overview&lt;/alt>
  &lt;/image>
&lt;/fig></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p><b>Result:</b> If the <codeph>&lt;img&gt;</codeph> element's width and height are both
            larger than <b>100 × 100 pixels</b>, the converter generates an
               <codeph>&lt;image/&gt;</codeph> element with the placement attribute as break and
            wraps it in a <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph> element. The converter also generates the
               <codeph>&lt;title&gt;</codeph> element from the image filename. The
               <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph> element is placed outside the preceding
               <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element so that the image is represented as a standalone
            figure.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
